window.FWN_REBORN_BOOT_CAMP_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_REBORN_BOOT_CAMP_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":5501,"title":"Chapter 5501: No Fate","paragraphs":["Xia Jinyuan felt helpless about his girlfriend’s honesty and sighed, \"If Third Brother knew you ignored everyone else, it would break his heart.\"","\"I won’t let Third Brother find out.\" Ye Jian smiled and winked, \"If I don’t say anything and you don’t say anything, Third Brother will never know. Speaking of which, is Third Brother also coming home for the Spring Festival this year?\"","\"I’m not sure, all I need to know is that my future father-in-law is coming back. Before you came down today, you talked to Old Man Xia about us extending our vacation and asked if my future father-in-law would come back for the Spring Festival this year. Old Man Xia then called to ask, and it was a security guard who answered, telling him that my future father-in-law would be on leave. At that moment, I felt like God was on my side.\"","Xia Jinyuan decided not to keep her in suspense, and seeing Ye Jian’s immediate relief, he glared at her with a mix of annoyance and amusement, \"Are you really that afraid of me bringing up the engagement to my future father-in-law?\"","Without disguising her feelings, Ye Jian nodded in reply, \"I am a bit afraid. You know my father plans to keep me at home until I’m twenty-seven or twenty-eight. If you suddenly bring up engagement, I genuinely worry my father will whip you with a belt.\"","\"As long as my future father-in-law agrees, I’d be willing to be whipped ten times.\" Taking advantage of the red light, Xia Jinyuan reached over and ruffled Ye Jian’s hair, \"Baby, I really can’t wait to marry you now.\"","\"If you have the chance, you would definitely discuss it with my father in advance.\" Ye Jian was certain of this, because the man beside her never picked a battle he couldn’t win.","\"Of course, I would ask my future father-in-law in advance, I wouldn’t overstep anyone, especially not my future father-in-law.\" Xia Jinyuan had never thought to play any tricks in front of his future father-in-law, because, he was very aware, that any slight scheming on his part would lead to unbearable consequences.","For example... if they could get engaged after another four or five years, that would also be fine!","Xia Jinyuan had a deep understanding of how formidable his future father-in-law could be. A soft knife that slowly cuts, grinding you down until you’re quaking in fear, and then, with a smile, he would sheathe the knife and say, \"Just kidding,\" leaving you so scared you nearly wet yourself, all the while maintaining his refined and graceful demeanor.","Such prowess was truly fearsome.","Seeing the remnants of trepidation on his face, Ye Jian, sitting in the passenger seat with one hand supporting her forehead, laughed until she couldn’t contain herself.","They left in the morning and returned at nightfall, driving up the mountain road that wound through the silence, surrounded by a vast expanse of white snow. In the expensive capital city, Dan Gui Garden felt like a paradise.","The entire Dan Gui Garden was exceptional in its stillness. Passing several villas, each household was quiet, with red lanterns hanging outside their doors, casting a festive glow that faintly diminished the night’s austerity.","A car approached from the front, and as the two vehicles passed side by side, Xia Jinyuan, focused on driving and talking to Ye Jian, did not notice who the other driver was.","Qin Xiu, however, saw Xia Jinyuan in the light of the headlights, slowing down his speed also let him see Ye Jian in the passenger seat, smiling like a blossoming flower.","Qin Xiu’s hands tightened on the steering wheel, recalling what Qin Ying had said during the day, he let out a barely audible sigh within the car, filled with a bitter taste.","As his sister had said, if it’s not meant to be, it’s not meant to be, harboring it in one’s heart is futile.","The cars passed each other, driving off in opposite directions, just like Qin Xiu and Ye Jian, destined to be an unrequited love on Qin Xiu’s part, never to bear fruit.","\"It’s getting late now, I won’t go in and disturb Grandpa Gen. You should rest early.\" Xia Jinyuan kissed Ye Jian’s forehead and then pecked her lips firmly."]},{"number":5502,"title":"Chapter 5502: Waiting","paragraphs":["Ye Jian’s face blushed unseen in the dark night, but she did not dodge anymore, until Xia Jinyuan let her go, \"Be careful when driving on the road, don’t drive too fast.\"","\"Mm, I’ll come over to pick you up tomorrow morning.\" Xia Jinyuan smiled again as he kissed Ye Jian’s forehead, reluctant to leave, \"Rest early, goodnight.\"","\"Mm, you should also rest early, goodnight.\" Ye Jian, with her hand covering her flushed face to cool it down, carried the bags inside the door, while Xia Jinyuan stood behind her until she entered the family home.","When Ye Jian returned home, she saw the dim lights in the living room. She initially thought the Old Man Xia had already gone to sleep, but unexpectedly, Old Man Xia was still sitting in the living room watching TV.","Ordinarily, Old Man Xia would go to bed at nine in the evening. It was just a bit past nine now. Uncle Fu had urged him once, but Old Man Xia said he wanted to wait for Ye Jian to come back, so Uncle Fu stopped urging and stayed to wait with him.","Seeing Ye Jian return, Uncle Fu immediately stood up from the sofa, \"You’re back, eh? Are you tired?\"","At home, Uncle Fu was always like an elder to Ye Jian, gentle and kind, always caring for her.","Old Man Xia smiled even more kindly, \"Our princess is back. Come, let Grandpa see what you’ve gathered today.\" Anticipating her return, Old Man Xia was happy to wait.","Ye Jian didn’t expect that Old Man Xia and Uncle Fu were both still awake, and she was immediately filled with guilt. She dropped her bags to the floor and sat down next to Old Man Xia, embracing his arms, \"Grandpa, my apologies for making you wait, I will make sure to come back earlier next time.\"","It was past nine and they hadn’t slept, surely because they were worried about her and were waiting.","\"I haven’t waited long, haven’t waited long, I just wanted to see what you’ve got today.\" Old Man Xia observed Ye Jian wearing clothes completely different from when she left, nodding with a smile, \"New clothes, did Little Six pick them out for you? He has good taste, they look nice.\"","Ye Jian pointed at the handbags on the floor, moving closer to Old Man Xia and spoke teasingly, \"Grandpa, when do I not look good? Look, all bought by him, I didn’t even want to buy them, and he was not happy about it.\"","Making her boyfriend look good, it couldn’t be helped, they were getting engaged after all.","It was surely necessary to give Grandpa some peace of mind.","\"Yes, that’s true, our Fu family’s granddaughter looks beautiful in anything.\" Old Man Xia agreed wholeheartedly with Ye Jian’s self-praise. In his eyes, his granddaughter was the best girl, incomparable to anyone, \"Why didn’t Little Six come in for a cup of tea before leaving? It’s late in the night, it shouldn’t be a problem, we have guest rooms at home.\"","He wasn’t an outsider, he was definitely going to be the grandson-in-law, staying over for one night at home wouldn’t be an issue.","\"We all thought Grandpa had already gone to sleep, so he didn’t dare to come in and disturb,\" Ye Jian softly said, \"Tomorrow he will come to our home and play chess with Grandpa.\"","\"Little Six is thoughtful, that’s good, the way he takes care of you, Grandpa is also very reassured. It’s getting late, and you must be tired too, go and rest early,\" Old Man Xia slowly stood up, \"Tomorrow Little Six will come over, he will surely take you out again.\"","Ye Jian helped Old Man Xia to stand, \"Tomorrow we might go to the horse track, but it’s not decided yet, if we go to the horse track, would you like to come with us, Grandpa?\"","\"Hahaha, silly girl, you two go out and have fun, I’m just an old man, why join the fun? If you go to the horse track tomorrow, have a good time. It’s rare to get a rest day, and it’s during New Year’s too, you must have fun, that’s the proper way.\"","The old master certainly didn’t want to follow; the young folks had their way of having fun. If he went along, he might spoil their fun."]},{"number":5503,"title":"Chapter 5503: Guard","paragraphs":["Ye Jian couldn’t accept that, \"Grandpa Xia, Grandma Xia are going, how can you not go?\"","\"That’s just to humor you two. At my age, going to the horse farm, I can’t ride, and I’d just be a burden on you kids to accompany me. I won’t enjoy it, so I won’t go, I won’t go.\" Old Man Xia was skeptical; he knew the couple too well.","\"If Grandpa Xia and Grandma Xia really go, then you must go too. Xia Yunyin’s horse farm is warm; there’s a chess room and a tea room. You can sit inside and watch us ride from the big French windows. Next door, there’s a pattern shooting range, also Xia Yunyin’s place; you could play there for a day.\"","Other old masters might not be tempted, but the idea of seeing his granddaughter ride a horse was very exciting for him, so he asked, \"And the shooting range? Can I see that?\"","\"Yes, yes, yes.\" Ye Jian hurriedly assured, \"You can see everything from inside.\"","The old master was thoroughly convinced, \"Sounds like a nice place. That Xia family’s fifth brother is pretty capable, finding such a place. If the Xia couple goes, then grandpa will join them too.\"","\"But let me make it clear beforehand, you play your games, but please don’t just stay inside because grandpa is there, neglecting to play.\"","\"Okay, I’ll definitely not just stick around, I’ll make sure to have fun. Let me take you back to your room, and we can confirm tomorrow whether we’ll go or not.\" Ye Jian, smiling, helped Old Man Xia back to his room. Seeing her happy made him happy too.","His granddaughter was so thoughtful!","After escorting Old Man Xia back to his room, and having finished washing up, Ye Jian lay in bed with no trace of sleepiness, her mind filled with Xia Jinyuan’s words about their engagement.","The thought always made her nervous; not that she was unwilling to confirm her relationship with Xia Jinyuan. Of course not, she was willing, and they had already met each other’s parents. It was really just a matter of having an engagement ceremony in front of both families and holding a wedding.","She understood very clearly that in this world, she couldn’t find anyone more suitable for her than Xia Jinyuan. Given a second chance at life, this man had become an inseparable part of her world, and she was well aware of his feelings for her.","From acquaintance to love, they had spent so many years together, and it was time to settle down, first getting engaged, then married; step by step, it was actually quite nice.","The Xia family was a hundred percent supportive; the only worry was her own family. Grandpa was easy to talk to, but her father would take some effort. However, Captain Xia said he’d handle it.","Alright, she would let him handle it first. If he couldn’t, she would step in. This would also show Captain Xia’s sincerity, letting her father see his true intention to be with her for a lifetime.","Thinking about it, Ye Jian’s heart settled again.","Her cellphone on the nightstand suddenly rang. Ye Jian immediately got up from the bed, grabbed the phone quickly.","It was a message from Xia Jinyuan, letting her know he had gotten home safely.","Ye Jian returned the message with a smile, \"Okay, get some rest early, see you tomorrow.\" After replying, she hugged the phone and laughed, no different from any other girl with a crush.","Xia Jinyuan, who had just returned to the Xia family’s old residence, was also in a good mood replying, \"Hmm, see you tomorrow. Sweet dreams.\"","\"Tsk tsk tsk, seeing this, one can tell you had a fulfilling day.\" Xia Yunyin, who had been waiting for him to return, approached with a smile, \"What do you think, isn’t the idea your fifth brother gave quite good?\""]},{"number":5504,"title":"Chapter 5504: Making Trouble","paragraphs":["Xia Jinyuan put away his phone, and even the tenderness at the corners of his eyes completely dissipated. He glanced indifferently at Xia Yunyin, who became visibly uneasy, \"What... what kind of expression is that? Don’t tell me, you had a fight? No, that’s not right; the way you were just now, like you’re on an aphrodisiac, it didn’t seem like a fight at all.\"","\"Little Six, today I was severely lectured by grandma, so don’t you scare me. I’m faint-hearted and can’t take fright!\"","This concerned Little Six’s lifelong happiness and the pressure on him as an elder brother was immense. He was terrified of inadvertently ruining Little Six’s chance at a happy marriage.","After a long while, Xia Jinyuan finally let out a cold \"Hmph,\" \"Fifth brother, keep those ideas to yourself and your girlfriend. Who tries, who knows.\"","\"How are things at the horse ranch? Are we still going tomorrow?\"","His Little Fox liked horse riding and shooting; as for shopping, she really had no interest in it.","Upon hearing that nothing was amiss, Xia Yunyin instantly felt a sense of relief, as if he had eaten a heart-calming pill, \"The day after tomorrow, let’s go the day after tomorrow. Tomorrow I will have someone tidy up the horse ranch well and straighten out the shooting range thoroughly, and we will go over again the day after.\"","\"I’ll also invite some friends, all from the social circles of the capital city. It’s good for you and your sister-in-law to meet and get to know them.\"","Just as Xia Jinyuan was about to agree, he suddenly became vigilant, \"Is there a reason for this?\"","A family outing wouldn’t cause the fifth brother to invite friends from his circle in the capital city for no reason. The friends from the capital city weren’t ordinary friends; each one was either rich or noble.","\"This afternoon, I had two friends call me, saying their mothers had just been inquiring about the Xia family, especially mentioning Little Six. My friends were alert and probed further, and, lo and behold, they found out that my former aunt has been out playing the victim again.\"","\"Now, most of the ladies in the circle know Little Six as the scoundrel who disowns his biological mother. I tell you, Little Six, that mother of yours really can’t stay out of trouble. She schemed against me a few years back, and when that failed, she kept quiet for a while only to stir up trouble again. Your days, I’m afraid, won’t be too peaceful.\"","With a mother holding you back, how can your days be peaceful?","On hearing this, a fierce rage filled Xia Jinyuan’s eyes, darker than the night itself, but soon he regained his composure, \"There’s more to this. Madam Xiao is now trying to recognize me; she wouldn’t do anything that would put her at a disadvantage.\"","\"Are you saying someone is taking this opportunity to make trouble?\" A chill came over Xia Yunyin’s handsome face, and the once cheerful man suddenly revealed a ruthless side only seen in the business world, \"I’ll investigate. Once I find out, I’ll take good care of them.\"","\"Fifth brother, there’s no need to investigate. I’ll meet with your friends tomorrow and see, oh, and do any of your friends happen to be married? If so, please invite their wives over as well.\"","Xia Jinyuan didn’t want to drag Xia Yunyin into the mess. He already had an idea of who was behind the trouble.","\"You have a lead? Can you handle it yourself?\" Xia Yunyin sensed what was left unsaid, feeling somewhat reassured.","\"Mm, one who is not very easy to deal with, but also poses no significant threat. The waters are somewhat deep, and as a businessman, you are not suited to get involved.\"","Xia Jinyuan hinted just enough.","\"Alright, as long as you’re confident.\" The hint was enough for Xia Yunyin to understand that the matter was beyond his means to solve. He was capable, but it wasn’t appropriate for him to step in.","As for what Xia Jinyuan requested, Xia Yunyin could guarantee with assurance. In the capital city, what he had the most was friends: those related to business, mere acquaintances, a few genuine ones, and several who had grown up together and were now successful in their own right. Xia Jinyuan could bring as many friends as he wished to the gathering; Xia Yunyin could arrange that many friends to attend."]},{"number":5505,"title":"Chapter 5505 The Same","paragraphs":["Xia Yunyin left the task to Xia Jinyuan, who felt completely at ease. After chatting for a few more sentences, Xia Yunyin received a phone call and quietly slipped away from the Xia family’s old residence.","Before he left, he didn’t forget to remind Xia Jinyuan to cover for him.","Xia Jinyuan waved his hand, signaling him to leave quickly.","Receiving a call late at night and acting all secretive, it was clear there was something fishy—probably off to some den of vice to enjoy himself.","Xia Jinyuan was well aware and didn’t bother to meddle. He knew his brother’s character through and through; Old Fifth was carefree and tended to spend money like water, but he indeed knew how to earn it. The money was his to spend, and he wouldn’t do anything terrible. On the other hand, if there was a good deed to be done, he could be counted on to take part.","During university, one of his classmates fell gravely ill. The classmate came from a remote village, and it was no small feat for him to have continued his education through high school. The illness was undoubtedly a disaster for the whole family. Later, it was Old Fifth who generously lent a hand. Now, despite being stationed far on the border, that comrade never forgot to write letters to Old Fifth, expressing gratitude for the second chance at life he gave him.","The Xia family had never been one to forget their roots. Each member had their own moral boundaries; they were clear on what was acceptable and what was absolutely off-limits.","Among the siblings in the family, only the fifth brother was the exception, an eccentricity he inherited from their uncle—genetics at play, unchangeable.","After Xia Yunyin left, Xia Jinyuan washed up and went to bed, careful not to disturb the old master and Old Madam who had retired early for the night. It wasn’t until the next day, early in the morning, that he appeared in the courtyard, startling the old master who was practicing Tai Chi.","\"How come you’re at home?\" The old master relaxed his stance, extremely surprised to see his grandson at home, \"Didn’t you go with Little Ye yesterday? How come you’re back already?\"","Xia Jinyuan was also troubled, feeling like all the elders in his family were hoping they’d go out.","\"I came back last night; you and grandma had just gone to rest. I’ll head to Dan Gui Garden after breakfast.\" Xia Jinyuan walked to the center of the courtyard and began practicing Tai Chi alongside his grandfather. \"It’s been a long time since I’ve practiced. Take a look and see if my moves are up to standard.\"","The old master, hearing that his grandson would be visiting Dan Gui Garden later, felt reassured. Seeing him actually practice, the old master was invigorated. \"In the past, you didn’t want to practice with me. Now that I’m not inclined to have you join me, you insist on doing so.\"","\"Your posture is wrong, why are you raising so high? Trying to lift the sky? It should be level with your shoulders, and your horse stance needs to be stable. If your lower body isn’t firm, how were you trained in the unit? You haven’t practiced well yourself, and yet you have the nerve to lead the team?\"","The old master was strict, and by the end of the Tai Chi sequence, Xia Jinyuan had broken out in a warm sweat.","Old Madam watched from a distance for a long time but didn’t go over to disturb the pair. The grandfather, grandson, and grandmother trio were cheerful and harmonious in the courtyard adorned with red plum blossoms defiantly blooming despite the snow.","Over at the Fu family in Dan Gui Garden, very early in the morning, the security guards and Uncle Fu were cleaning up together in preparation for New Year’s Eve. With \"Fu\" character posters and paper-cuts for window decorations and large red lanterns hung around, the place had a festive Spring Festival atmosphere.","Ye Jian joined in the effort, cleaning the furniture and mopping the floors upstairs and downstairs, even occasionally humming a few military songs, clearly enjoying herself immensely.","Singing \"We soldiers are unique in our own way,\" Old Man Xia from downstairs immediately continued, \"It’s because we are all wearing simple uniforms.\" Ye Jian’s laughter raised in volume as she sang, \"We soldiers are unique in our own way...\" Just after finishing the phrase, Uncle Fu and a security guard, who were cleaning in the courtyard, came in and joined in singing, \"Though we say we’re different, actually we’re quite the same, all in the prime of youth, stout-hearted lads.\"","One could say that the house was filled with soldiers!"]},{"number":5506,"title":"Chapter 5506: Worry","paragraphs":["Old Man Xia had been in the air force, Ye Jian was in the army, Uncle Fu had once been an air force quartermaster, and the security staff were Chinese military police. After finishing their song, Old Man Xia burst into laughter, \"When your brother comes back, our family will have the sea, land, air, and military forces all represented!\"","Wiping the stair handrail all the way from the second floor to the first, Ye Jian, smiling brightly, added, \"Wrong, Grandpa, there’s also the tactical police. Have you forgotten Niannian?\"","\"Hahaha, yes, yes, yes, girl, give Niannian a call and ask if she has time to come over to our house. When your brother is home, we should invite Niannian more often.\"","Old Man Xia genuinely liked Zhou Niannian’s personality; she was like a little sun, perfectly warming up their family’s icy exterior grandson. One was warm like sunlight, the other as steady as a mountain, an ideal match!","Years had passed, and Old Man Xia hadn’t given up his initial thoughts.","Ye Jian also wanted to invite Zhou Niannian over, but while wiping a vase with several branches of Red Plum in it, she asked unsurely, \"I don’t know if Niannian has a boyfriend; if she does, it might be inconvenient.\"","\"If she has a boyfriend, then Grandpa will stop thinking about it. None at all, Grandpa has been paying attention,\" Old Man Xia, although retired and at home, still had connections. Old Man Xia, who never used these connections, had specially asked someone to keep an eye out for Zhou Niannian’s situation for his grandson Li Jinnian’s lifelong happiness.","Knowing Zhou Niannian didn’t have a boyfriend, Old Man Xia was relieved.","Ye Jian admired Old Man Xia’s foresight deeply and performed a salute from the TV shows, pressing one fist in the palm of the other hand, and bowed to Old Man Xia from afar.","Old Man Xia, now in good health and with a younger mindset, responded in kind to Ye Jian and, like an erudite hermit, said with a smile, \"Don’t admire me too much, Grandpa has eaten more salt than the water you’ve drunk. This matter won’t stump Grandpa.\"","Uncle Fu listened and could not help bursting out a laugh, though he didn’t have the heart to embarrass Old Man Xia.","Indeed, such matters would never vex Old Man Xia; the key was that he had never used his connections to handle family affairs in his life. Concerned about gathering information on Miss Zhou Niannian, Old Man Xia thought it over for three nights and discussed it with Old Master Qin for half a day before making that call.","In Old Man Xia’s words, for his grandson’s happiness, he was willing to put his old face on the line!","The hands-off Old Man Xia just needed one phone call, and the person at the other end expressed joy the following day by visiting to say that doing a small task for Old Man Xia was his honor.","Zhou Niannian indeed had no boyfriend because she was always waiting for someone, waiting for that person to take more initiative, just a bit more effort, and she would definitely turn into a fireball to give that fellow a good searing, then slowly roast and handle him afterward.","In four days, it would be Chinese New Year’s Eve. Uncle Fu was preparing to go out to buy some food supplies needed for the New Year, along with some fresh fruits and gifts for New Year’s visits. Ye Jian, expressing great interest, felt that as a member of the family, she should also be involved in preparing the New Year goods, so she went along with Uncle Fu, and, worried about Xia Jinyuan visiting and finding no one, she specially made a phone call.","Xia Jinyuan was having breakfast with Old Master Xia and Old Madam Xia, on hearing this, he put down his chopsticks and smiled, \"That’s a good idea, we can go to the horse farm tomorrow. Let’s go buy New Year goods today.\"","He wanted to continue to spend time with Ye Jian, but Ye Jian quickly said, \"No, no, no, you should stay with Grandpa Xia and Grandma Xia. I haven’t even visited the two elders since coming home, and yet I’m always monopolizing their grandson, which isn’t nice.\""]},{"number":5507,"title":"Chapter 5507: Doting Love","paragraphs":["Old Madam wanted to hear Ye Jian’s voice, and as soon as Xia Jinyuan said it was Ye Jian calling, she signaled him to put it on speaker. Hearing Ye Jian’s thoughtful words, Old Madam laughed until she couldn’t close her mouth, saying again and again, \"Girl, your grandparents don’t need any company, let Little Six keep you company. It’s rare for you two to meet, your grandparents can’t monopolize Little Six.\"","Old Madam’s kindly voice came through the phone, and Ye Jian was still a little nervous. Both Old Madam and the old master were very kind. Ye Jian greeted the two elders’ health with poise first. Old Madam and the old master smiled around the phone, exchanging intimate words with Ye Jian.","\"You, it’s rare for you to be home for family festivities. If I remember correctly, this is only the second time you’ve spent New Year’s at home. Last time, you left on either the second or third day of the New Year. Little Ye, don’t worry about Grandma Xia or Grandpa Xia, we’re both in good health. You don’t have to worry, just keep your grandpa company and have a happy New Year.\"","\"Your fifth brother said he’s tidying up the horse farm today; he’ll invite you all to play tomorrow. If you have time, go have fun; if not, after the New Year is also fine. Ten days of holiday should be enough.\"","Commander Xia really liked the righteous spirit Ye Jian possessed and even those clear, glass-like pure black eyes. He always told Old Madam that such pure eyes only belonged to the best of children, and if Little Six could marry Little Ye as his wife, it would be a great fortune for the Xia family.","As the head of the family, Commander Xia had a keen eye for people, and if he said so, he was naturally not wrong.","Old Madam was also sharp in judging people. The first time she saw Ye Jian, she had already decided Ye Jian would be her granddaughter-in-law. Now seeing that Xia Jinyuan and Ye Jian were affectionate despite the long distance, the two elders were relieved and did not want to hold up the couple’s reunion by keeping them company.","For them, reunions were too difficult, and as elders, they had to be understanding.","On the other side, Ye Jian, nodding continuously, said, \"I’m preparing to visit the New Year’s market to do some shopping. My father and my brother are both coming home this year. Indeed, it’s going to be a joyous New Year. Grandpa Xia, Grandma Xia, my brother and I will pay a New Year’s visit to you two elders together later.\"","\"Hahaha, very good, very good. When you and your brother come over, our house will be even more lively,\" Old Madam was delighted, laughing while Xia Jinyuan made quiet gestures with his fingers, checking to see how deep the smile wrinkles at the corner of Old Madam’s eyes were.","Then, pretending to be jealous, he said, \"Your grandson is right here, right here. Please spare a few glances, if you would?\"","\"Go on, don’t be an obstruction,\" Old Madam Xia pushed away the head that Xia Jinyuan was leaning in with and continued to chat with Ye Jian, laughing heartily. The two elders set the phone down on the table and sat to each side, looking as if they could chat with Ye Jian for hours over the phone.","Old Man Xia watched with a chuckle.","Ye Jian was going to marry into the Xia family, and having a good relationship with the elders of the Xia family meant happiness for Ye Jian, and it made Old Man Xia even more at ease.","Knowing that Ye Jian was going to purchase New Year’s goods, Commander Xia and Old Madam chatted for about ten minutes before talking with Old Man Xia on this side, while Ye Jian went to the market with Uncle Fu.","The Spring Festival was drawing near. Streets everywhere were adorned with festive décor, and everyone was busy preparing to celebrate this reunion holiday, smiles on everyone’s faces. And all of this was because of the stability of the country.","The country’s stability was safeguarded by Ye Jian and the countless comrades-in-arms. Ye Jian had always been proud to be a soldier. She never regretted choosing this path, never regretted becoming a soldier, a Special Forces operative."]},{"number":5508,"title":"Chapter 5508: Loneliness","paragraphs":["Uncle Fu took Ye Jian to the oldest and most bustling ancient-style street in the capital city, which restored the architectural essence of the Ming and Qing dynasties. With all sorts of New Year’s goods fully stocked—food, utilities, decorations—it was a one-stop shopping experience, and Ye Jian found her eyes darting everywhere.","As Uncle Fu picked out ingredients, he chatted with Ye Jian, \"It’s truly wonderful that you all have come back. I’ve been with the Fu family for so many years, and I haven’t seen Old Man Xia as happy as he has been these past few days in a long time. Every year I want to stay and keep Old Man Xia company, but he’s always reluctant, instructing the security to book my ticket early and personally escorting me to the airport. An Jiaxin, Old Man Xia is in great health now, and you have played a big role in that.\"","\"During the Spring Festival in previous years, your father could occasionally make it back for the celebrations. But most of the time, Old Man Xia was left to celebrate alone in the house. Although people like us are around, we aren’t blood relatives, and I could see the sense of loss in Old Man Xia’s heart.\"","\"Especially seeing the neighboring Qin family always bustling with activity during the New Year, Old Man Xia didn’t know how envious he was. So, when Old Man Xia learned that you would stay for the New Year along with your father and Li Jinnian, he was so excited last night that he couldn’t sleep.\"","Hearing this made Ye Jian feel bittersweet. She hoped that Grandpa Gen could live many more decades, allowing her to take good care of him, \"From now on, I will try my best to make time to come back and spend New Year’s with Grandpa.\"","But some things aren’t as easily achieved as one might hope. The New Year’s she could spend with the elderly might become fewer and fewer, so she resolved to try her best to return every Spring Festival to be with Grandpa Gen.","\"Old Man Xia will certainly be very happy to know this,\" Uncle Fu said with a smile that crinkled his eyes, \"It doesn’t matter when, coming back for the New Year is certainly lively, but coming back any time is just as good. To Old Man Xia, whenever you come back, it’s like celebrating the Lunar New Year.\"","\"I’m really grateful to you for always being there with Grandpa, and for taking care of him on behalf of me and my father. Thank you, Uncle Fu. With you around, we are all very relieved while out on the team.\" Ye Jian sincerely appreciated Uncle Fu; without his attentive care, how could she be at ease?","Uncle Fu chuckled heartily, \"No need to thank me, no need at all. Old Man Xia is my benefactor, and taking care of him is the greatest honor of my life. There’s no need for thanks. Saying ’thank you’ would be too formal.\"","The Huahua Market was crowded, and while Uncle Fu continued talking, he picked out items, occasionally asking for Ye Jian’s opinion on things like couplets and paper-cuts. Whatever Ye Jian liked, Uncle Fu would agree to.","After choosing the couplets, Ye Jian suddenly remembered something, \"Will many people come to visit Grandpa Gen for New Year’s greetings? The last time I was home, quite a few guests came from the Space Academy.\"","\"Yes, yes, this year there might be even more. Students from the laboratory at the school, every year a few representatives and leaders will come. From the first day of the lunar month to the fifteenth, our home is full of people. Everyone knows Old Man Xia usually celebrates the Spring Festival alone, so many of Old Man Xia’s old friends, including former students, come to visit him,\" Uncle Fu answered earnestly, also to put Ye Jian at ease, \"Old Man Xia also likes having guests over, to drink tea and chat, it’s the liveliest time.\"","\"He won’t even need to cook as the food will be prepared by the security canteen and delivered. Old Man Xia just needs to make a phone call in advance to arrange it.\""]},{"number":5509,"title":"Chapter 5509: Family Affairs","paragraphs":["Speaking of the household matters, Uncle Fu, who was away from home, hadn’t paid much attention when he was at home. At home, the Old Man kept a close eye on him, forbidding him to talk too much and burdening Ye Jian with worries.","Once outside, however, Uncle Fu was free to speak his mind, naturally only sharing the good news and not the worries. Mainly because, at home, there really wasn’t any bad news to tell, except for the minor concerns when the Old Man occasionally caught a cold or coughed.","\"Everything is quite convenient at home. Besides me taking care of the Old Man, the security guards and their team are very attentive, too. You really don’t have to worry about the household. Take good care of yourself in the squad, and the Old Man will be even better,\" he said.","Uncle Fu, the duty officer who had cared for the Old Man for the longest time, had long regarded him as his own elder and, being about the same age as Chief Engineer Fu, had come to honor the Old Man as his own father due to his fatherless childhood.","Several times the Old Man had mentioned adopting Uncle Fu as a son by choice, but Uncle Fu never agreed. After all, he had a whole host of heedless relatives at home, including his underachieving son and daughter-in-law, who had once sneaked into the capital to seek a favor from the Old Man, infuriating Uncle Fu to the point of nearly disowning them.","Nevertheless, he ultimately felt indebted to his family and sometimes had no choice but to endure it.","Ye Jian was unaware of these matters.","Uncle Fu also didn’t want to mention his family affairs in front of Ye Jian and always avoided it, especially during the Spring Festival when he was worried she might ask about his family.","So, Uncle Fu started joking again, \"This year is truly great. In the past, those who came to pay New Year’s visits often brought their younger family members, and the Old Man felt quite sour in his heart. But this year, with the young lady keeping the Old Man company to entertain guests, the Old Man won’t feel jealous anymore.\"","Ye Jian pursed her lips and smiled. It seemed that her identity as a member of the Fu family would be hard to conceal this Spring Festival. If word got out, it would surely shock many people, like Madam Li and Madam Qin.","Old Master Li had passed away, and the biggest threat had been removed. Ye Jian no longer intended to hide her identity as the Old Man’s granddaughter.","There was no need for explicit explanations; letting things take their course was best.","Ye Jian followed Uncle Fu around all morning before finally carrying bags big and small back to Dan Gui Garden. Next door, the Qin household seemed to be livening up as security guards bustled in and out.","A security officer told Ye Jian that Old Master Qin didn’t want to spend the Spring Festival in the hospital and insisted on returning home. His family couldn’t persuade him otherwise and had to let Old Master Qin spend the festival at home, but they still took special care to have a nurse and a doctor accompany him.","The Old Man laughed and shook his head, \"It’s true, the older you get, the more you become like a child, so willful.\"","\"Old Master Qin probably feels more comfortable at home during the Spring Festival. After all, having his son-in-law visit for the first time and spending the occasion in the hospital would be somewhat inauspicious,\" Uncle Fu said with a laugh as he consoled the Old Man. \"Don’t worry. With nurses and doctors at home to provide care, nothing will go wrong. If you’re really concerned, we can visit later. An Jiaxin can accompany you.\"","Upon returning to Dan Gui Garden, it was usually the case that Ye Jian would not step out of the Fu family’s gate. This time, however, she had been to the Qin house, so Uncle Fu could surmise something.","The Old Man’s granddaughter no longer needed to hide.","That was certainly the case. The Old Man nodded and said to Ye Jian, \"Your father must be on his way back now. Just now, Grandpa Xia mentioned to me that we should take advantage of the New Year with both elders present to set the wedding date, and have a simple engagement ceremony. Little Six must have talked to you about this too, right?\""]},{"number":5510,"title":"Chapter 5510: Old Friend","paragraphs":["Grandpa Xia mentioned on the phone, and Old Man Xia wasn’t surprised at all. The two young people had been talking for years, and it was completely reasonable for them to get engaged now. It’s just that, well...","Deep down there was still a reluctance to let go.","Once engaged, in a few years, they would get married, and once married, his granddaughter would become another family’s daughter-in-law.","No matter how well-off the Xia family was, the thought of his granddaughter marrying away always left a sour feeling in his heart, and it hurt.","Ye Jian could see the reluctance and heartache hidden in the Old Man’s smile. She gently hugged his arm and said in a soft voice, \"He mentioned it to me yesterday, but I didn’t agree. I wanted to ask for your and Dad’s opinions first.\"","She spoke very cautiously, and that kind of careful prudence brought both comfort and pain to the Old Man. This child was always so considerate of the family, even at the expense of her own happiness.","\"When your Dad comes back, we’ll discuss this matter properly. It’s a big issue and needs to be carefully considered. Your brother, yes, we need to wait for your brother to return as well, so the whole family can discuss it together.\" Although the Old Man was reluctant, the Xia family’s Little Six was a talented young man and a worthy candidate for her to entrust her life to, so settling things early wasn’t necessarily a bad thing.","Gently patting the back of Ye Jian’s hand, he said, \"Silly child, in front of Grandpa, you can say whatever you want. You don’t need to worry about Grandpa; whatever you do, Grandpa will support you.\"","\"You and Little Six have been together for so long now, getting engaged is good. Our two families can also feel more at ease. Little Six is a good kid, responsible and loving towards you. With you and Little Six together, Grandpa is reassured.\"","Ye Jian’s eyes reddened, and she nodded obediently.","In the afternoon, Ye Jian accompanied the Old Man to visit Old Master Qin at the Qin family. Having just returned from the hospital, Old Master Qin appeared spirited and said to Old Man Xia, \"You have no idea how miserable the doctor was. I would rather lie at home than be willing to go to the hospital again.\"","\"You old fool! What kind of talk is that during the New Year!\" Old Madam, who had just relaxed, changed color in her face upon hearing the old master’s words. To come out of the hospital only to talk about lying down again was an uncomfortable thought to hear.","She slapped Old Master Qin’s shoulder forcefully and said to Ye Jian, \"Your Grandpa Qin here can really wear people out. The doctors and nurses were all at their wits’ end with him. It’s better now he’s back, so he won’t be troubling others.\"","\"What do you mean, ’won’t trouble others?’ I dislike troubling others the most. Clearly, I said yesterday to discharge me quickly, but it was you, Xiu, Ying, who disagreed, insisting I stay another day for observation. When the younger ones have pleaded, what more could I say?\"","Old Master Qin glared at his wife, resolutely refusing to take the blame, \"Coming home early would have been fine. Don’t I know my own body? It’s you all who make a fuss over nothing.\"","\"Grandpa Qin, the day you fainted really scared Grandma Qin. If it hadn’t been for Qin Xiu, Grandma Qin might have fainted from shock,\" Ye Jian intervened on behalf of Grandma Qin, hoping the three elders would take better care of their health in the future, \"From now on, in snowy weather, you can’t go running in the snow or anything like that. Just a stroll will do, and you need to dress warmer.\"","Grandpa Qin patted his forehead, joking, \"Oh dear, oh dear, another little Tang Monk has appeared. These days are going to be worrisome.\"","\"Deserved!\" Grandma Qin glared at her old man and then affectionately took Ye Jian’s hand, \"Your Grandpa Qin just needs to be told off. You should scold him more for Grandma Qin, and I’ll give you a big red envelope for New Year’s.\"","Ye Jian, with a twinkle in her eyes, nodded vigorously and took on the responsibility, \"Okay, I’ll definitely keep an eye on Grandpa Qin and my own Grandpa. They’re just like two kids, if not watched closely, I really worry they won’t take care of themselves.\""]},{"number":5511,"title":"Chapter 5511: Return Home","paragraphs":["Ye Jian naturally sided with Old Madam Qin, as it concerned the elderly lady’s health; she definitely needed to keep a close watch.","\"That’s right, that’s right, just like a child; you don’t get it yet, and you let us worry,\" Grandma Qin said, laughing so hard she could hardly close her mouth. What a good child, truly worthy of being a descendant of the Fu family. Even though raised outside, she was top-notch.","Their grandson, alas, why was he always a step late?","Qin Xiu was tidying up a room downstairs. Old Master Qin and Old Madam had always lived upstairs, but when the doctor suggested that the elders move downstairs, Qin Xiu immediately complied and quickly arranged the room.","Now that with the three elders was Ye Jian, who had always been beloved by them, Qin Xiu felt very relieved.","They chatted until about three in the afternoon, and seeing that Qin Xiu had tidied up the room, grandfather and granddaughter headed home, all smiles.","When night fell and the big red lanterns outside were lit, Ye Jian suddenly heard the sound of a car in the Fu family courtyard, and as if by instinct, before the guard could open the door, she ran like a tornado towards the entrance.","\"Hey, hey, slow down, slow down, don’t fall,\" Old Man Xia, coming out of the kitchen, quickly cautioned her. Seeing that Ye Jian was headed towards the main entrance, he asked the security officer who had arrived.","The guard smiled and said, \"A car stopped in the front yard, not sure who it is yet.\"","As the front door opened, Ye Jian saw Chief Engineer Fu, travel-weary with luggage in hand, standing at the entrance, raising his hand in a motion to ring the doorbell.","\"Dad!\" Ye Jian jumped for joy, wearing only a thin sweater, bouncing in front of Chief Engineer Fu. Her girlish playfulness was on full display the moment she saw him—a child at that moment, happy and blissful.","Chief Engineer Fu was even more surprised; he really hadn’t expected that his daughter would be at home, too. He dropped his luggage to the ground and caught his daughter as she jumped into his arms, his laughter echoing with joy, \"An Jiaxin! Oh, my precious daughter is also home for the Spring Festival! Hahaha, it’s a good thing dad got leave, or else I’d have missed it again!\"","Seeing his daughter, Chief Engineer Fu’s eyes brimmed with excitement. His research task for the Spring Festival had come to a pause, and considering that it had been years since he spent the festival with his old father, he had applied for holiday leave for the Spring Festival and hurried back home.","He never expected that his beloved daughter would also have come home for the Spring Festival.","Old Man Xia, hearing the commotion and coming outside, saw the father and daughter still standing at the entrance. The tearful old man leaning on his cane thought, They’re back, they’re all back now.","\"This year we can finally have a lively New Year. It won’t be just this lonely old man celebrating anymore. Li Jinnian should be almost home too; then it will truly be a reunion.\"","Old Man Xia continued, \"Rest of our lives, come inside quickly. Haven’t you noticed our little princess is dressed thinly? Hurry, come in first, then we can sit down and talk.\" After saying this, he called out to Uncle Fu, who was busy in the kitchen, \"Uncle Fu, quickly, cook a smoked fish for your big brother; he loves it the most!\"","Uncle Fu, still stir-frying in the kitchen and not hearing anything, was informed by the security officer who jogged to the kitchen. Uncle Fu came out immediately with his spatula in hand, seeing Chief Engineer Fu, he raised the spatula as his hometown accent slipped out, \"Ah, what a comfortable day! Rest of our lives, you must’ve come back just in time for dinner! Get one, I’ll make a smoked fish right now! It’s going to be delicious!\"","Chief Engineer Fu happily nodded his head, \"Good, good, good, I’ll have to trouble my big brother again! It’s not just coincidence, I timed it just right to come back for dinner!\""]},{"number":5512,"title":"Chapter 5512: Worrying about","paragraphs":["Uncle Fu, holding the spatula, became even more joyful, \"Haha, not bad, won’t let yourself go hungry. Xiao Yu, come here, give your uncle a hand.\"","Xiao Yu was a guard, and had a very good relationship with Uncle Fu as well. Upon receiving the order, guard Xiao Yu immediately entered the kitchen, happily lending a hand.","The Fu family had a total of three guards on duty this year, with Xiao Yu on shift. The other two guards had been given leave by Old Man Xia, who specially went to the guard company to ask the company commander for a one-month annual leave for the guards who hadn’t been home for four years. When Ye Jian returned home, the other two guards had just left for three days.","Chief Engineer Fu, with a chill in his body, vigorously rubbed Ye Jian’s head. My, his precious daughter was so happy her eyes were all but invisible, \"Dad will go upstairs to change clothes first. I’ve been at the base for half a month and left directly with my luggage. This smell on me, I’m afraid it might smoke you out.\"","Once in the lab, sometimes busy for ten days or a half month, hygiene time was truly squeezed out for the sake of experiments.","It was precisely because of researchers like Chief Engineer Fu who worked tirelessly, even putting their health aside, that our country’s military strength grew stronger year by year.","\"Alright, alright, go change your clothes, don’t smoke out Jian girl,\" Old Man Xia’s smile never left his face, \"After you change, it’ll be just in time for dinner.\"","Chief Engineer Fu responded and when he went up the stairs, he took several steps in one stride, going up the stairs quickly to wash up; his silhouette radiating joy no matter how you looked at it.","Ye Jian was always smiling. How nice it was that the family could celebrate the New Year together, now only big brother was missing. She would call her brother’s mobile phone later to see if she could reach him.","\"I just don’t know when your brother will be back. He shouldn’t suddenly have something preventing him from returning, right?\" Old Man Xia also thought of Li Jinnian, and couldn’t help but mention it. These past few days, he had been looking forward to his son and granddaughter returning for the New Year, and had not even made a phone call to ask if his grandson could truly make it home this year.","\"I’ll send a message to my brother later to ask. If he can make it, he should be home in these next two days,\" Ye Jian said smilingly, her entire being exuding the scent of happiness, \"Then our family will really have a reunion New Year.\"","\"Hahaha, yes, yes, after dinner you contact him and see,\"","\"Okay, Grandpa, you take a seat first, don’t stand there.\"","\"I’ve been sitting all day; it’s good to stand.\"","\"Then let me help you, just now you were telling me not to fall, but you are the one who should really be careful.\"","\"How about we ask your brother now?\" The grandfather who was concerned about his grandson abroad still wanted to confirm early, \"When he sees your message, he will definitely call back right away.\"","Ye Jian immediately took out her mobile phone from her pocket and swiftly sent a text message, not sure if her big brother’s phone was with him, but if he could see the message, he would likely call back.","Just after the text message was sent, before Ye Jian could put her phone back in her pocket, it vibrated. Both granddaughter and grandfather burst into laughter.","\"It must be your brother!\" Old Man Xia was so happy that he hurriedly sat down on the sofa, \"You answer the phone, you answer the phone.\"","It was indeed Li Jinnian calling. He was about to turn off his phone as he had just boarded the plane, but upon seeing the message, he truly called Ye Jian back immediately.","A cool and distant voice came through, \"Are you also at home for the New Year?\" There was a hint of hard-to-detect joy; the usually reserved man was rarely so expressive of his own emotions.","After glancing at Ye Jian’s text message, he was almost certain that Ye Jian was at home at that moment."]},{"number":5513,"title":"Chapter 5513: Gathering Together","paragraphs":["Hearing the familiar voice, Ye Jian quickly turned on the speakerphone so that Old Man Xia could hear Li Jinnian’s voice. On the other side, Li Jinnian heard Ye Jian’s laughter, joyous as a mountain spring.","\"Brother, guess where I am?\"","\"Talking with Grandpa.\" A smile touched Li Jinnian’s handsome brows as he looked out the airplane window at the bright lights and peaceful scene, knowing his sister was also at home, waiting for his return.","\"Impressive! I didn’t even say, but you guessed it. Where are you now? Grandpa is really hoping you’ll come home for New Year’s.\" After saying this, Ye Jian even winked at Old Man Xia, who laughed heartily.","What a sturdy girl!","\"At the airport, about five hours from home.\" No sooner had Li Jinnian spoken than he heard Old Man Xia laughing and saying, \"Everyone is coming back, everyone is coming back. Little Fu, prepare a few more dishes. Jinnian will want something to eat even in the middle of the night.\"","Even though Uncle Fu was busy, he was all smiles, \"Alright, alright, I’ll prepare Jinnian’s favorite dishes right away. When he was a boy, he loved steamed pork with rice flour, I’ll make him a big bowl tonight.\"","Not yet home, yet the thick, warm affection washed over him from the other end of the phone.","On the plane, other passengers were also on their phones, invariably telling their families that they were on board, each bubbling with happiness. Those away longed to return home, while those at home eagerly awaited their return.","With about twenty minutes till takeoff, Li Jinnian checked his watch, then asked Ye Jian when she had gotten home and how much holiday she had.","\"I’ve been home for five days already. I was originally given only three days off, and that too because I passed through the capital city. Then suddenly, I don’t know how, they gave me an extra ten days on a whim, just enough to spend a good New Year with Grandpa. Brother, how many days do you have?\"","\"I have fifteen, enough to also spend New Year’s with Grandpa, even a few days more than you,\" Li Jinnian said softly, a light smile on his brows, relaxing against his seatback. \"Tell Uncle Fu not to work too hard, just one steamed pork will do.\"","\"Uncle Fu is in a happy mood now, my father just came back, and Uncle Fu happily added more dishes.\"","\"Uncle-in-law is back?\" Li Jinnian sat up straight, a smile emerging in his cool eyes, \"This is definitely going to be Grandpa’s happiest year.\"","Exactly, Ye Jian looked toward Old Man Xia, who had stepped into the kitchen and was instructing enthusiastically. Her face radiant and bright as the sun, \"With you coming back, Grandpa will be even happier.\"","Old Man Xia poked his head from the kitchen and called out to Ye Jian, \"Tell your brother to ask his father to come to Dan Gui Garden if he’s free.\"","Now that Old Master Li had passed away, it was Li’s turn to handle affairs. His daughter’s husband... well, he was a pitiful man. Never mind, for the sake of his grandson, it was better to keep relations warm.","The Li family had dispersed, and the son-in-law’s return would hardly be lively, especially since Madam Li least expected her son-in-law to come home. Jinnian’s return made it essential to at least visit his biological father. The relationship between father and son was lukewarm, and face-to-face meetings hardly meant much. It was better to spend New Year’s together.","Ye Jian didn’t know Li’s Uncle-in-law very well, she had not even met him. Upon hearing this, she faithfully relayed Old Man Xia’s words, \"Brother, what about Uncle-in-law? Grandpa said to invite Uncle-in-law to come to Dan Gui Garden for New Year’s. It’s warmer with more people.\"","With Old Man Xia speaking up, Li Jinnian would never object. He was silent for a while before he finally spoke, \"Okay, I’ll ask.\"","In past years, when Old Master Li was still alive, if his father came back, he had to spend Lunar New Year’s Eve with the Li family. But this year, after Old Master Li’s demise, he didn’t want to go to the Li family’s old residence and deal superficially with Madam Li."]},{"number":5514,"title":"Chapter 5514: Heartless","paragraphs":["They didn’t get along, so there was no need to make themselves sick over the holidays.","Up until now, the relationship between Li Jinnian and his father was marked by a mutual understanding—don’t trouble me and I won’t trouble you, live your own lives. But with Old Man Xia having spoken up, Li Jinnian asked whether they would celebrate the New Year together, though he was not particularly concerned.","After Li Jinnian ended the call, he made a call to Old Master Li.","It wasn’t Old Master Li, but rather his second wife, who answered the call. As she saw the incoming call on the phone, her gaze flickered slightly before picking up.","\"Hello, Jinnian,\" she said just one sentence, and the gaze of Madam Li sitting opposite her was sharp and venomous, shooting straight across.","This scourge, why would he contact the Boss?","Could it be that the father and son’s relationship had thawed?","Hearing his stepmother’s voice, Li Jinnian immediately lost the desire to speak. The stepmother knew it too, and said, \"Just hold on,\" before handing the phone to her husband who was coming out of the washroom, whispering, \"It’s Jinnian’s call.\"","Old Master Li’s expression darkened slightly as he took the phone his wife passed to him and began coldly, \"What is it?\"","It was less like a father and son and more like strangers.","Li Jinnian had long since become accustomed to this and conveyed Old Man Xia’s message in a flat tone as he awaited Old Master Li’s response.","Old Master Li first snorted coldly, then spoke in a chilly voice, \"You belong to the Fu family; where you go is none of my concern. Tell Old Man Xia, I won’t come over to be an eyesore.\"","After saying this, he ended the call and said to his wife authoritatively, \"You need not bother with his calls.\"","The stepmother was also used to her husband’s indifference towards his eldest son, giving a low \"mhm\" in agreement without fussing further.","He was the son left by the first wife; the less involved he was with her husband, the more it played to her and her own son’s advantage.","Madam Li, who had listened to the entire conversation, felt relieved knowing their father-son relationship remained cold.","\"Alright, Boss, you know Jinnian has always been closer to the Fu family, so there’s no reason to be upset. Later on, when Ronghuan comes back, you should ask him what exactly he plans to do. Does he really expect me to kneel before him, this old bone, for him to let me go?\"","As the eldest son, Old Master Li might have favored his second wife but hadn’t treated his eldest son unfairly. And Madam Li might have had her small schemes against Old Master Li, but she was wary. Now she dared to move against Li Ronghuan yet didn’t dare to make a move on Old Master Li.","And see, with Li Ronghuan causing trouble, she still had to call on the first wife’s eldest son.","Old Master Li was very much like Old Master Li, even in his cold nature. Old Master Li always said that Li Chuhai had the same ruthlessness in his bones as him, so Old Master Li’s coldness was a legacy of the Li family.","To Old Master Li, family affection was just this and nothing more.","No matter how much Li Ronghuan made a fuss, as long as it didn’t affect him, Old Master Li would not intervene.","Reacting to his stepmother’s words, Old Master Li said indifferently, \"Whether he makes trouble or not is not for me to decide. What needs to be said, I will say.\"","\"You are his elder brother; naturally, he will listen to your advice,\" Madam Li said without a pleasant expression. \"Tianhao, now that your father is gone, are you planning to bully me, this old thing, like Li Ronghuan does?\"","Li Tianhao was Old Master Li’s name.","\"You’re overthinking it,\" Old Master Li glanced coldly at his stepmother, \"You can still live in the Li residence, when have I ever said anything? If I truly acted, would you still be able to stay in the Li household?\"","\"Li Tianhao!\" Madam Li was so angry she slapped the table, \"How can you talk to my mother like that! This is her home, are you planning to drive her away?\""]},{"number":5515,"title":"Chapter 5515: Not Easy","paragraphs":["Madam Li did not act impulsively and even advised her daughter to calm down before saying to Old Master Li, \"Tianhao, when I entered this family, I never thought about leaving.\"","\"You don’t have the capability to drive me away either. I’ve managed everything in this household for a lifetime, taking care of everything inside and out. Even though you have become successful now and are turning around to drive me away, if you really do this, I won’t let you off easily.\"","Old Master Li smiled lightly, gesturing for his wife to pour him a glass of water, indicating he needed to have a good talk with his stepmother.","Meanwhile, Ye Jian received a message from Li Jinnian, confirming that her never-before-seen father-in-law would not be coming to Dan Gui Garden for the Spring Festival.","When Old Man Xia found out, he wasn’t disappointed; he had always known that his son-in-law was cold-hearted. He had disagreed with his daughter marrying him from the start, seeing through that his son-in-law was not a good man.","Such a cold man, yet his daughter had insisted on marrying him back then, only to end up covered in wounds before she slowly realized she had entrusted her life to the wrong person.","What she thought was love was merely her own wishful thinking.","Well, if he doesn’t come, then let it be.","\"He won’t come, then he won’t. We’ll just wait for your brother to come home, and then the family will be all together,\" said Old Man Xia, not letting this affect his mood. His son-in-law was no longer considered part of the family, only there for the sake of his grandson Jinnian.","He remembered the times when Old Master Li was still around; the son-in-law naturally had to return to the Li family’s old residence for the Spring Festival. With the pillar of the family, Old Master Li, gone, only Madam Li was left. She had never gotten along with her stepchildren, and now with the old master gone, the lack of a balancing force meant that some disturbances at the dinner table on New Year’s Eve wouldn’t be surprising.","Having his son-in-law over for the New Year’s dinner was something Old Man Xia considered carefully, not wanting Li Jinnian to worry over any fuss caused by the Li family.","Since the son-in-law was unappreciative, he let it be.","After freshening up, Chief Engineer Fu came down, and Ye Jian chirped around him like a songbird, chattering non-stop. Chief Engineer Fu, extremely patient, always responded with a smile to whatever Ye Jian asked.","\"There are only those few days of the New Year, traffic jams from the base to the airport, and jams from the airport in the capital city back home, all rushing home for the New Year.\"","Old Man Xia smiled, \"The Spring Festival, our country’s biggest holiday, those who work away from home all rush back and naturally the roads are congested.\"","\"Nowadays, our country’s transportation has developed; highways, railways, airplanes—we have it all, far stronger than our time. I remember one year rushing back to the capital city for the New Year, starting with a bike ride to a village and staying overnight at a villager’s home, then early next morning taking the villager’s donkey cart to the town, from there a tractor ride to the city, and then a car to the provincial capital city’s train station—and only then finally catching the train home.\"","\"Just traveling took a whole week. Later, your grandma and I never went back to the capital city for the New Year again. Your dad and your aunt stayed at a villager’s home till they were ten before grandpa sent them back to the city to live in a boarding school.\"","Those times were tough but had a sense of hope; no matter how hard or unbearable it was, we clenched our teeth and survived.","In his childhood, Chief Engineer Fu recalled, \"During New Year’s when other children were looking forward to it, your aunt and I weren’t at all. Other families had festive and joyful New Years, our house was so cold that ice formed on the walls.\"","Remembering hardships only made the sweetness clearer; Chief Engineer Fu did not hide the hard times of the past, just wanted Ye Jian to understand that, compared to then, every day now was a good day."]},{"number":5516,"title":"Chapter 5516: Mention","paragraphs":["Chief Engineer Fu had known hardship as a child; sometimes, he didn’t even have enough food for three meals a day.","\"Dad was fifteen before he saw his grandpa three times, but saw his grandma a bit more, about once a year. The rest of the time, he stayed with family friends or at school, and during the New Year, we went to the military base. Sometimes, when my sister and I really missed our grandparents, we each brought a comforter and cried secretly inside the bedding, careful not to let anyone hear us.\"","\"We most often spent the New Year at the Qin family’s home; even our new clothes were prepared by Old Madam Qin. My sister and I used to wonder why our mom and dad couldn’t work at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.\"","The Fu and Qin families had been friends for decades. Old Man Fu and his wife were both researchers on secret projects. Upon learning this, the high-ranking leaders instructed their subordinates to take good care of the brother and sister.","Even though they were raised without their parents’ constant presence, Chief Engineer Fu and his sister still received an excellent upbringing and developed fine characters.","But after all, it wasn’t the same as being at one’s own home, as comfortable as it could be.","Ye Jian was deeply attracted to the profound struggles of those bygone years, when real hardship meant that even returning home was difficult. Unlike today, where travel has made coming home from far and wide much simpler.","In another ten years, there would be even better transportation.","As the New Year approached, many people were still traveling home, and the streets of the Capital City were still terribly congested. Ye Jian, Chief Engineer Fu, and Old Man Fu chatted while waiting for Uncle Fu to serve the food.","As they talked, the conversation shifted toward the topic of Ye Jian and Xia Jinyuan.","Old Man Xia started the conversation, mentioning the engagement between Ye Jian and Xia Jinyuan, \"Since you’ve returned and have a few days of leave, now that the whole family is together, let’s settle the matter between little Jian and Little Six.\"","\"You know what kind of young man Little Six is; his abilities and character are both top-notch. He and our An Jiaxin have been in a relationship for so many years, sharing the same ideals, trusting each other thoroughly as combat partners at work, and you’ve seen the affection between the two children. Why not take advantage of the New Year to get them engaged? It would be a joyful occasion for the entire family.\"","\"Engaged? Dad, how did you suddenly think of engagement? An Jiaxin is still so young, how long has she returned to the Fu family? How can her lifelong affair be decided so quickly? I still want to keep little Jian with me for a few more years. No, no, she definitely can’t get engaged so soon,\" Chief Engineer Fu said, frowning and immediately objecting, \"I had already told Little Six that An Jiaxin wouldn’t get married so early.\"","\"She’s just returned to the Fu family after so many years; how can she simply become someone else’s family member? Dad, I can discuss other matters, but I cannot agree to this one. Getting married early means she becomes someone else’s daughter-in-law,\" Chief Engineer Fu shook his head repeatedly. His precious daughter who just returned to his side, how could she be pried away so easily?","He hadn’t had enough time with her yet! Even an engagement was out of the question! Thinking about his daughter becoming someone else’s family through marriage, Chief Engineer Fu felt as though his heart was bleeding.","Xia Jinyuan wasn’t wrong, the greatest obstacle to the engagement was Chief Engineer Fu.","Old Man Xia had anticipated Chief Engineer Fu’s opposition and chuckled, \"Just because she’s your treasured daughter, doesn’t mean I don’t treasure my granddaughter. I see that the young man from Xia family is suitable, and both the old master and Old Madam Xia like our little Ye Jian. That’s why I thought it would be good to get the engagement sorted out early, it’s not a mistake.\"","\"Isn’t it just having a few more people to care for our little Jian? And our An Jiaxin likes the Xia family boy too. Engagement and marriage are both inevitable, and since everyone is at home, why not settle it while we’re at it?\""]},{"number":5517,"title":"Chapter 5517: Debate","paragraphs":["Old Man Xia agreed, and Chief Engineer Fu’s gaze turned especially mournful—how could he return home to hear such explosive news?","He started to doubt... Had he come home too timely? If Little Six from the Xia family hadn’t come home, there definitely wouldn’t be any engagement.","Why did this boy have to come home for the New Year this year?!","Ye Jian was feeling a bit bitter, but when she suddenly saw Chief Engineer Fu’s mournful gaze, she wanted to laugh again.","Old Man Xia continued his earnest persuasion, \"Moreover, no matter where Ye Jian marries and lives in the future, she will always be our Fu family’s daughter. How did she become someone else’s now?\"","\"I really don’t like this kind of talk. Even if Ye Jian gets married, she will forever be my Fu family’s daughter. Just because she’s married doesn’t mean she’s no longer her own family! This way of thinking is incorrect and needs to change!\"","By the last sentence, Old Man Xia had become very serious, his voice particularly stern, his face even set in a frown.","Chief Engineer Fu, with a pitiful and mournful gaze, glanced at his daughter and then said to Old Man Xia, \"Dad, I know what you mean, but just look at our girl—how old is she now? It’s really not good for the marriage to be settled so early.\"","\"You also said that Little Six from the Xia family really likes our girl. Since that’s the case, waiting another two years should be fine.\" Chief Engineer Fu understood Old Man Xia’s point, but he just didn’t want to settle the matter so soon.","He thought about how his long-cherished daughter would soon become someone else’s wife, and nothing in his heart felt right; everything was uncomfortable and distressing.","The family’s cabbage was about to be taken by the pig!","Old Man Xia had a headache looking at his son, who appeared to be quite single-minded and unassailable in his conviction. How is it that this boy, grown so big, couldn’t even be reasoned with anymore?","\"Ye Jian and Little Six are just talking about an engagement, not about getting married and registering right away. It’s something the kids are happy with, so what’s there for you to be unhappy about?\"","\"Dad, I really am not objecting. I agree to both the engagement and the wedding. It’s just that I think it’s too soon. An Jiaxin just graduated last year, and it’s only been a year since she started working—how could she get engaged so early? Let’s delay for another two or three years. By then, I’ll definitely agree!\" Chief Engineer Fu was also trying to reason with Old Man Xia.","This matter required getting the old father to unite with him on the same front; they could not allow the enemy to split them into two opposing forces. At any rate, the family had to stick together!","He agreed to the engagement; it was only the timing he disagreed with!","\"Are you perhaps still hoping that a better son-in-law will come along, one who’s even more suitable? So, you don’t want to rush into having Ye Jian engaged just in case it becomes a shackle! Look at your father, Ye Jian! Has he gone senile? I am nearly ninety years old and not as confused as he is!\"","Old Man Xia was actually getting angry at Chief Engineer Fu.","Chief Engineer Fu hurriedly tried to placate Old Man Xia, \"Dad, Dad, Dad, please calm down, I’m not thinking about someone better or more suitable. In my heart, Little Six is the better and more suitable one, definitely the only choice for son-in-law. Accusing me of such—this is a true injustice!\"","\"I am really not disagreeing, nor do I have too many complicated thoughts. I simply and naively think the engagement is just a bit early. Our Jian is only twenty-three years old. She went to school early and graduated early. In your school, aren’t there people who graduate at the age of twenty-three? And even those who are a bit older are still graduate students, still students.\"","\"You can’t just because the two have been dating for a few years, assume that the time spent dating is enough to move on to engagement. We have to consider their actual ages and can’t switch concepts.\""]},{"number":5518,"title":"Chapter 5518: Turn Against","paragraphs":["Old Man Xia was working on persuading people, and Chief Engineer Fu was no exception. Originally it was a matter concerning Ye Jian and Xia Jinyuan, but in the end...","Ye Jian glanced at Old Man Xia, and then at Chief Engineer Fu. She sneakily sent a text message to Xia Jinyuan, which read, \"Be ready for my dad to bombard you.\"","Knowing that Chief Engineer Fu would disagree, she had not expected him to be so adamant.","Chief Engineer Fu, who was steadfast in his opinion, continued to persuade Old Man Xia, \"In two more years, An Jiaxin will be just twenty-five. I’m absolutely not opposed to an engagement. It’s not that I’m against it; I just think it’s a bit early.\"","\"Do you really feel comfortable with An Jiaxin getting engaged at twenty-three? If it were one of your students, wouldn’t you advise against it? You would, right? Twenty-three is so young. To get engaged so early, ah, Dad, I honestly think it’s too soon.\"","Then...","Xia Jinyuan replied to his girlfriend’s text message, \"How is your future father-in-law now? Did he get angry?\"","Ye Jian peeked at Old Man Xia and, covering her laugh, replied to the message, \"The situation doesn’t look good. It seems like my dad has thoroughly convinced Grandpa Gen. Initially, Grandpa agreed to the engagement, but now, I’m afraid he might side with my dad.\"","Upon seeing the message, Xia Jinyuan: \"...\"","His future father-in-law really was a talent; he was practically ready to kneel before him.","Old Man Xia had initially agreed, but in the end, he was swayed.","Xia Jinyuan’s respect for his future father-in-law grew even more in that moment.","Ye Jian, seizing the right moment, spoke up, \"Dad, Grandpa, let’s not discuss the engagement for now; let’s eat first. We can talk about this matter calmly; I’m not in a hurry. I’m really worried that because of my business, Dad and Grandpa will argue.\"","Ye Jian was genuinely worried. During the New Year, if her dad and grandpa argued over her engagement, it would truly be her fault.","\"Your dad is just a stubborn mule!\" Despite feeling irritated inside, Old Man Xia couldn’t help but curse Chief Engineer Fu a couple more times, yet he felt there was some truth in his words.","Considering their age, it seemed that his granddaughter’s engagement was indeed a bit early.","Perhaps they should wait and discuss it later?","\"Grandpa, please don’t be angry. I know you all want what’s best for me. For that reason alone, please, Grandpa, don’t stay mad, okay?\" Ye Jian held Old Man Xia’s hand, comforting him, \"My dad really doesn’t mean anything else. Don’t be angry. He just can’t bear to let me go.\"","Old Man Xia glanced at his son, who was trying to appease him with a smile, and let out a somewhat relieved \"hmpf,\" \"I’m just afraid he’s eyeing the bowl but thinking about the pot.\"","Chief Engineer Fu couldn’t help but show a bittersweet expression, \"Dad, I really don’t mean that. It’s just An Jiaxin is too young. I don’t want her to get engaged over the New Year.\"","Going home for the New Year only to have a bucket of cold water dumped on you unexpectedly, Chief Engineer Fu felt a deep chill in his heart.","Getting engaged, waiting another two years isn’t too late!","Uncle Fu, carrying steaming dishes, came out, \"Come, come, come, dinner’s ready, dinner’s ready.\"","This year, with the family accompanying Old Man Xia for New Year’s, his joy led him to instruct the guard to open a bottle of red wine, and to the guard Xiao Yu he said, \"Xiao Yu, you stay this year. Come, don’t just stand there, join us! Next year, I’ll give you holiday time, so you can go home early for a joyous New Year.\"","Xiao Yu came from Yun Province and was a rural kid. To get home in Yun Province, he still needed to take a bus to the town, then a motorcycle ride, and finally... walk for about five hours to reach his home.","For him, staying in the capital city for the New Year was a mark of Old Man Xia’s appreciation. His family, knowing this, reminded him to take good care of Old Man Xia and not miss home too much.","With a simple smile, Xiao Yu said, \"Old Man Xia, I’d be even happier to spend New Year’s here. Next year, I’ll still stay put. As long as you’re willing to keep me on as your guard.\""]}]);
